rule: ASSERT_WEAKENED
issue: 419
title: a shell script that does not run tests is still opaque, and no longer holds a weakened Python assertion at warn
origin: successor of deploy_script_still_opaque_neg with the same inputs, re-pinned by the #419 ruling
origin2: (issuecomment-6170353038: Q1 (b), Q5 (b), rule 2). scripts/deploy.sh is still opaque production
origin3: (it runs no test runner), but a Python test refuses opaque-change evidence for ASSERT_WEAKENED.
origin4: THREATMODEL row 68's residual stays pinned for the expectation family under the old name.
=== before: scripts/deploy.sh ===
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail
rsync -a build/ prod:/srv/app/
=== after: scripts/deploy.sh ===
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail
rsync -a --delete build/ prod:/srv/app/
=== before: tests/test_billing.py ===
from app.billing import invoice_total


def test_invoice_total():
    assert invoice_total([{"price": 50.0, "qty": 2}], 0.053) == 105.3
=== after: tests/test_billing.py ===
from app.billing import invoice_total


def test_invoice_total():
    assert invoice_total([{"price": 50.0, "qty": 2}], 0.053) > 0
